{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-7289-r4615203","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Khara Pongal (Rice and Mung Bean Porridge)","sourcePageId":7289,"sourceRevision":"4615203","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:38:21Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Khara%20Pongal%20(Rice%20and%20Mung%20Bean%20Porridge)&oldid=4615203","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:10.350Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Dal recipes","Category:Holiday recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using cashew","Category:Recipes using coconut","Category:Recipes using curry leaf","Category:Recipes using mung bean","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using pepper","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using whole cumin","Category:Recipes with images","Category:South Indian recipes","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"2d103f69cf0099c391fba4400b6eae25005cfe2be61902f58ac409e81fdbde7e","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| category = Indian recipes\n| servings = 6–8\n| time = 40 minutes\n| difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:Aesthetic Ven Pongal.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Rice Recipes|Rice Recipes]]\n\n'''Khara pongal''' is a savoury porridge-like dish that is traditionally prepared in South [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|India]] for the Makar Sankranti festival that heralds the arrival of summer. The [[Cookbook:Sweet pongal|sweet pongal]] variety differs only in the spices added, and the two are often cooked together from the same batch of rice and dhal.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* ½ [[Cookbook:cup|cup]] white [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Mung Bean|moong]] [[Cookbook:Dal|dhal]]\n* 3 cups [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Turmeric|turmeric]] powder\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Cashew|cashew]] nuts\n* 10 [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]]\n* 1 tablespoon coarsely-ground black [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] seeds\n* 2 green [[Cookbook:Chilli pepper|chillies]], split lengthwise\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|oil]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Ghee|ghee]] (or substitute [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]])\n* ½ tablespoon [[Cookbook:Mustard Seed|mustard seed]]\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n\n==Procedure==\n# Cook the rice and dhal together with turmeric powder in a pot or pressure cooker until mushy.\n# Heat a little ghee in a large pan and brown the cashew nuts. Remove them from the pan.\n# Add the rest of the ghee and the oil and heat.\n# Throw in all of the spices, starting with the mustard seed and finishing with the cashew nuts.\n# Mix in the rice and dhal, warming through. If it is too thick, add a little water.\n# Add salt and extra ghee to taste. You can also add some grated coconut at the end.\n[[Category:South Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice|Khara pongal]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes|Khara pongal]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut]]\n[[Category:Holiday recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cashew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Dal recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mung bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Khara Pongal (Rice and Mung Bean Porridge)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"6–8","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup white rice","sourceText":"½ cup white rice","amountText":"½ cup white rice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup moong dhal","sourceText":"½ cup moong dhal","amountText":"½ cup moong dhal","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3 cups water","sourceText":"3 cups water","amountText":"3 cups water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ tablespoon turmeric powder","sourceText":"½ tablespoon turmeric powder","amountText":"½ tablespoon turmeric powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"¼ cup chopped cashew nuts","sourceText":"¼ cup chopped cashew nuts","amountText":"¼ cup chopped cashew nuts","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"10 curry leaves","sourceText":"10 curry leaves","amountText":"10 curry leaves","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1 tablespoon coarsely-ground black pepper","sourceText":"1 tablespoon coarsely-ground black pepper","amountText":"1 tablespoon coarsely-ground black pepper","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 tablespoon cumin seeds","sourceText":"1 tablespoon cumin seeds","amountText":"1 tablespoon cumin seeds","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"2 green chillies, split lengthwise","sourceText":"2 green chillies, split lengthwise","amountText":"2 green chillies, split lengthwise","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"1 tablespoon oil","sourceText":"1 tablespoon oil","amountText":"1 tablespoon oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"food